OpenRevo @VERSION@ for Debian and Ubuntu
======================================

This package contains the ordinary-user desktop application and the EC
driver source. Install it using apt to resolve its declared dependencies.
The package scripts never invoke apt themselves.

Configuration delegates module registration, compilation, installation,
and signing to the distribution DKMS helper. On the running host the
installer then activates the module and refreshes permissions only for
/dev/openrevo_ec. Active local sessions receive access through uaccess.
The GUI itself does not run as root.

The package also includes openrevo-cli. It connects to the running desktop
in the same user session; it does not start a separate service or open EC
hardware. Run openrevo-cli --help for mode, fan, battery and status commands.
The Rust runtime renews fan leases even with the window hidden in the tray.
Applied mode and custom power settings are saved automatically. Startup and
configuration import do not apply settings. A CLI timeout does not cancel
an operation; inspect status before deciding whether to retry.

The result is recorded in /var/lib/open-revo/driver-status.json. A ready
result requires the installed and loaded module source versions to match,
a bound device, and verified read/write access for the active local user.
This file records the last configuration attempt, not continuous health.

On upgrade, an identical loaded srcversion is retained. A changed module
is removed only through normal modprobe -r. If in use, it is left loaded
and a reboot is requested. No forced unload is performed. Package removal
unregisters only the package's exact DKMS version and does not unload an
active module. An already loaded module may remain until reboot.

An installed application can report ready=false:
- Missing running-kernel headers: install linux-headers-$(uname -r), or
  reboot into the newly installed distribution kernel with matching headers.
- Secure Boot signing-key rejection: inspect mokutil --sb-state, enroll the
  distribution DKMS MOK as described by the distribution, then reboot.
- No supported EC device: standard monitoring is available; the kernel
  driver requires MECHREVO vendor and the Uniwill WMI GUID. Inspect sudo journalctl -k.
- No active local session: log in locally with systemd-logind running.
- /etc/dkms/no-autoinstall: review this administrator policy explicitly.
- Chroot or container: DKMS can build but activation and device permissions
  are deferred. Configured DKMS activation hooks must be reviewed first.

After resolving an outstanding condition, retry:
  sudo dpkg --configure open-revo

For a package already marked configured, rerun the explicit helper:
  sudo /usr/lib/open-revo/driver-setup configure @VERSION@

Genuine DKMS build/install failures, unexpected command failures, and
manual duplicate modules fail configuration. Duplicates under
/lib/modules/<kernel>/extra/openrevo/openrevo_ec.ko (including compressed
variants) are reported and preserved for explicit administrator handling.
No package script removes arbitrary old module files.
